Z||000004||Archie||07-20-2001||09:29 PM||||Wow, that thing has to be a collectors item.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>It was produced in late 1990. Had about 5000 made and (in the olden days of snail mail and very few Fiero shows) everyone of them was distributed via mail in request.<P>The Henry Ford Museum contacted me about 3 months ago asking for my oldest literature for some project they were working on. I went thru a bunch of old files and found one in an old envelope that had been returned as undeliverable.<P>Boy, remember the old days when brochures were designed by people WITHOUT computers & to mail something you had to put a stamp on it?<P>We are working on a new mailer right now and the initial proofs look real good.<P>Thanks for the offer, Aus.<P>Also thanks for bringing back the memories.<P>Archie||||reg||1
